14 Mill Wynd is within the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not listed and has no tree preservation order.

Our guidance says replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So if you want to change the material (for example, timber to uPVC) or the glazing pattern or style, you will likely need to apply. If the replacements are exact matches, you may not need to.

I can't give a formal opinion on whether your specific proposal needs permission. To confirm, please contact the planning desk with details of the current windows and the proposed replacements, or submit a pre-application enquiry.
